---
import ResourceAbout from "../../components/ResourceAbout.astro";
import LearningGuideLink from "../../components/LearningGuideLink.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import AgenticNav from "../../components/AgenticNav.astro";
import LearningEngineeringFlower from "../../components/LearningEngineeringFlower.astro";
import cases from "../../../public/agentic-le/cases.json";
import run from "../../../public/agentic-le/replay/live-exemplar.json";
import workforce from "../../../public/agentic-le/replay/workforce-conversation.json";
const workforceProduct = "/agentic-le/cases/workforce-conversation/";
const originalCases = cases.cases.filter(c => !c.iteration_of);
const displayedCases = originalCases.map(original => {
 const iteration = cases.cases.filter(c => c.iteration_of === original.id).at(-1);
 return {...(iteration || original), original, refined: !!iteration};
});
const modelResponses = run.events.filter(e => e.kind === "request").length;
const artifacts = run.events.filter(e => e.kind === "artifact").length;
---
<Base title="Agentic LE · Capability Matters"
 description="From a seed idea to a runnable candidate product, with public agent discussion, scenario challenges, evidence and versioned artifacts.">
  <LearningGuideLink id="agentic-ai-lab" />
 <meta slot="head" name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
 <AgenticNav active="cases" />
 <header class="intro container-wide">
  <p class="eyebrow">Agentic learning engineering · Problems → Products</p>
  <h1>Explore learning engineering teams</h1>
<ResourceAbout resource="agentic-le" />
  <p>Configure complementary expertise around the learning engineering flower. Follow how shared understanding, contributions, and operating conditions shape a candidate design, then inspect the evidence behind it.</p>

 </header>
 <section class="container-wide lab">
  <section aria-labelledby="flower-heading">
   <h2 id="flower-heading">A shared framework for the experiments</h2>
   <p>Eight starting expertise domains surround shared understanding. Learners and other stakeholders remain connected to the whole team. Assign one or several domains to a member, share responsibilities, and select the expertise the challenge needs.</p>
   <LearningEngineeringFlower />
   <p><a class="studio-link" href="/agentic-le/dynamic/">Open dynamic design conversations</a> <a href="/agentic-le/roles/#comparisons">Understand the five comparisons</a></p>
   <p>Use two phases: dynamic Design / Develop conversations, then Deploy / Test under easy, medium, and hard conditions. Specialists have bounded responsibilities; the generalist has introductory cross-domain knowledge. An expert evaluator examines the complete conversation and observed result separately. Edit and export a case here, run it locally, then import the retained record. Earlier fixed-workflow results remain available below.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="cases" aria-labelledby="cases-heading">
   <h2 id="cases-heading">Earlier case records · {originalCases.length} problems · {cases.cases.length} runs</h2>
   <p class="case-note">Preserved agent execution on fictional problems, using the original team configurations. These replays are historical examples, not new flower study results. Each refinement keeps its original run available; human pilot approval and field evidence remain pending.</p>
   <div class="case-grid">{displayedCases.map(c => <article class="case-card" id={`case-${c.id}`}>
    {c.refined && <><span id={`case-${c.original.id}`}></span><p class="refinement-label">New product iteration</p></>}
    <p class="case-domain">{c.label.replace(" · live agents", "")}</p>
    <h3>{c.title}</h3>
    <p class="case-counts">{c.counts.request} model calls · {c.counts.artifact} artifact versions · {c.counts.scenario} scenario {c.counts.scenario===1 ? "challenge" : "challenges"}</p>
    <nav class="case-actions" aria-label={c.title}>
     <a class="replay-link" href={`/agentic-le/replay/?case=${c.id}&v=quality-6`}>Replay this case</a>
     <a href={`/agentic-le/replay/?case=${c.id}&view=conversation&v=quality-6`}>Join the meeting replay</a>
     <a href={c.product}>Try its candidate</a>
     <a href={`${c.product}product.zip`} download>Download record & product</a>
     {c.refined && <><a href={`/agentic-le/replay/?case=${c.original.id}&v=quality-6`}>Compare the original replay</a><a href={c.original.product}>Try the original candidate</a></>}
    </nav>
   </article>)}</div>
   <p class="source"><a href="/agentic-le/record/?file=%2Fagentic-le%2Fcases.json">Case inventory and journal hashes</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/blob/main/docs/lifecycle/CASES.md">Expansion checklist</a></p>
  </section>
  <section id="team" class="team-overview" aria-labelledby="team-heading">
   <h2 id="team-heading">Trace contributions into the design</h2>
   <p>Shared understanding means integrating domain concerns into requirements, decisions, implementation, and evaluation. Every team member has responsibility for the learners and stakeholders affected by the design.</p>
   <p><a href="/agentic-le/roles/"><strong>Explore the flower domains and shared responsibilities</strong></a>. The guide also preserves the original role contracts for interpreting historical replays.</p>
   <p>The scorecard examines <strong>human flourishing support, system performance, and learning</strong> separately. Ratings concern the design and available evidence. Claims about learning or impact require suitable evaluation with people.</p>
  </section>
  <p class="paper-link"><a href="/agentic-le/flower-study/"><strong>Inspect the earlier fixed-workflow study and its original evidence</strong></a></p>
  <p class="paper-link"><a href="/agentic-le/paper/"><strong>Read the preserved earlier pilot paper: Exploring the learning engineering flower with agentic simulation</strong></a></p>
  <div class="grid">
   <article><h2>Inside the workforce candidate</h2><p><strong>{workforce.seed.title}</strong> lets a new team lead compare authored openings, separate facts from explanations, and reconsider a proposal when protected time and coverage are withdrawn. Access, authority, capacity and agreement remain independent. Its reflection is descriptive; it does not assess employees.</p><p>The handoff contains executable HTML, requirements, versioned artifacts, the project journal and a source-linked manifest. It is a candidate product requiring affected-person review and field validation.</p><p><a href={`/agentic-le/record/?file=${encodeURIComponent(workforceProduct+"manifest.json")}`}>Inspect the product handoff</a> · <a href={`${workforceProduct}requirements.md`}>Read the requirements</a></p></article>
   <article><h2>The preserved original workforce record</h2><p>The saved fictional workforce project contains {modelResponses} model requests, including a rejected correction, and {artifacts} artifact versions. Scenarios changed interruption privacy and reviewer-conflict requirements. An actual missing-code finding reopened Build.</p><p>The replay preserves original drafts, dissent, prompts, provider metadata, failed validation and the corrected candidate. Recorded browser checks support only the behavior exercised in that environment.</p><p><a href="/agentic-le/record/?file=%2Fagentic-le%2Freplay%2Flive-exemplar.json">Inspect the source journal</a> · <a href="/agentic-le/replay/?case=workforce&v=quality-6">Follow the original workforce revisions</a></p></article>
  </div>
  <article><h2>From candidate to operational product</h2><p>Understand → Map → Design → Build → Instrument → Experiment → Evaluate → Refine is a revisitable cycle. Build produces the executable candidate; refinement can return to any invalidated requirement. The learning engineer integrates the work and keeps human and system requirements visible.</p><p>Real use needs accountable ownership, affected-person review, appropriate data handling, accessible operation, a meaningful comparison and stopping rules. Learning, workplace transfer and flourishing remain claims to investigate. Inadequate conditions can justify changing the product, changing the work system, or stopping.</p><p>The hosted site serves saved products and replay. New model runs use the local runner in this repository; hosted model access and a shared job queue remain future work.</p></article>
  <p class="source"><a href="/problems-to-prototypes/">Return to project seeds</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/tools/lifecycle">Runner source</a> · <a href="https://github.com/wrgr/capabilitymatters/tree/main/docs/lifecycle">Specification and operating documentation</a></p>
 </section>
</Base>
<style>
 .studio-link{display:inline-block;background:var(--ink);color:white;padding:.7rem 1rem;border-radius:5px;margin-right:1rem;font-family:var(--sans);text-decoration:none}.refinement-label{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.75rem;font-weight:700;color:#155948;background:#d4f4eb;padding:.35rem .55rem;border-radius:4px;width:fit-content;margin-bottom:.7rem}.team-overview{margin-top:2rem}.role-links{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;margin:1rem 0;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem}.role-links a{background:var(--tint);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:5px;padding:.55rem .75rem;text-decoration:none}.role-links a:hover{border-color:var(--accent)}#team{scroll-margin-top:7rem}#cases{scroll-margin-top:7rem}.intro{padding-top:1.4rem;padding-bottom:1rem}.intro .eyebrow{margin-bottom:.6rem}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.5rem);margin-bottom:.45rem}.intro p:last-child{max-width:52rem;margin-bottom:0}.lab{padding-top:.6rem;padding-bottom:3rem}.case-note{max-width:none;color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem;margin-bottom:1rem}.case-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.case-card{display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-width:0;background:var(--tint);padding:1.15rem}.case-domain{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:.7rem}.case-card h3{font-size:1.3rem;min-height:2.4em}.case-counts{font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}.case-actions{display:grid;gap:.45rem;margin-top:auto;font-family:var(--sans);font-size:.9rem}.case-actions a{width:fit-content}.case-actions .replay-link{background:var(--ink);color:white;padding:.45rem .75rem;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:.2rem}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.4rem}article{border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:8px;padding:1.4rem;margin-bottom:1.4rem;background:var(--bg)}h2{font-size:1.4rem;margin-top:0}.source{font-size:.85rem;max-width:none}.paper-link{margin:1.6rem 0}.lab a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent-2);outline-offset:3px}@media(max-width:760px){.case-grid,.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.case-card h3{min-height:0}.case-card{margin-bottom:0}.case-grid{margin-bottom:1rem}}
</style>
